	"_doc": "The sign library (SignLib): neon signs and holo ads any system can ask for by kind, tags and size. Fictional brands and generic words only, no real trademarks. kind: neon (lit tubes on a dark raceway, SignLib.STROKES) or holo (a translucent scanlined screen, holo.gdshader). form (neon): word, blade (stacked down a sign standing out from the wall), arrow (chasing bulbs, a word in it), icon (a picture, optionally a word under it), cjk (katakana, hangul or kanji words, real and plain). form (holo): logo (the name cycling with an emblem), ticker (scrolling text), dancer (a dancing silhouette), product (a can turning), screen (moving picture blocks), glyphs (an abstract glyph column), emblem, ad. tags: the places it suits (site kinds from sites.json, plus generic, street, sky). colors: tube or screen colours. anim: steady, flicker (a letter drops out now and then), broken (a dead letter, another sputtering), buzz (the whole sign hums), chase (bulbs running), cycle (holo). meaning: what the CJK says, so nobody hangs gibberish.",
